            "review_title": "Review at Leave Cafe",
            "review_text": "D P\nLondon, United Kingdom6 contributions\n0\ncosy wee cafe near Temple of Literature with musical twist\nNov 2016 • Solo\nStumbled upon this nice little cafe near the temple of literature. It has just opened and the staff were super friendly. Upstairs is a traditional music school teaching Vietnamese instruments like the Dan Tranh - a kind of zither.\n\nWas nice to enjoy a drink - i had a Vietnamese iced coffee with condensed milk which was good (definitely real coffee unlike some other cafes in the country) - and hear the traditional music being played at the same time. \n\nNo food at the cafe, just drinks.\n\nWould definitely go back as after a visit to the Temple of Literature this was a nice way to unwind and enjoy some more local culture in a more laid back setting. They had an English version of the menu and at least one of the staff spoke good English. \n\nThe area is also quite interesting, lots of places for lunch, and road also leads to the old national stadium - lots of activity round there. Well worth a look!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 2, 2016",
